hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18489","Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Amir narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn Mudarris al-Tai narrated to me, or informed me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the standing place and said: I came, O Messenger of Allah, from the two mountains of Tayyi, I exhausted my mount and wearied myself, and by Allah I left no mountain but I stood upon it, is there hajj for me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches with us this prayer and comes to Arafat before that by night or day, his hajj is complete and his unkemptness is ended."
"18490","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar, he said: I heard al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Harithah ibn Lam who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam and said to him: Is there hajj for me, so he said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer in this place, then stood with us in this standing place until the leader pours forth, having poured forth before that from Arafat by night or day, his hajj is complete and his unkemptness is ended."
"18491","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar who said: I heard al-Shabi narrating from Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned it."
"18492","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn al-Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Rawh."
"18493","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Safar who said: I heard al-Shabi, he said: Urwah ibn Mudarris narrated to us, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there hajj for me, so he said: Whoever prayed with us this prayer in this place and stood with us in this standing place until he pours forth, having poured forth before that from Arafat by night or day, his hajj is complete and his unkemptness is ended."
